---
import StarlightPage, {
	type StarlightPageProps,
} from "@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro";
import { Code } from "@astrojs/starlight/components";

const props = {
	frontmatter: {
		title: "AI agent access",
		template: "splash",
		description:
			"Learn how AI agents and LLMs consume Cloudflare documentation",
	},
	hideBreadcrumbs: true,
} as StarlightPageProps;
---

<StarlightPage {...props}>
	<p>
		Use this gude to grant AI coding assistants and LLMs access
		to Cloudflare documentation.
	</p>

	<h2 id="quick-start">Quick start</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>AI coding assistants (Claude Code, Cursor, Windsurf):</strong>
			Use the <a href="#documentation-mcp-server"
				>Cloudflare Documentation MCP Server</a
			> for a complete. It enables your assistant to search and retrieve
			documentation directly.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Agent Skills:</strong> Install
			<a href="#skills">Cloudflare Skills</a> into any skills-compatible AI tool
			for structured, task-specific guidance.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Chat interfaces (ChatGPT, Claude.ai):</strong> Append <code
				>/index.md</code
			> to any docs page URL and paste it into your conversation to receive
			Markdown instead of a full web page.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Project rules and custom instructions:</strong> Add a product-level
			<a href="#per-product-endpoints"><code>llms.txt</code></a> URL to your AI tool's
			rules file to give it an index of relevant Cloudflare pages.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>API-aware coding:</strong> Download the
			<a href="#openapi-specification">OpenAPI spec</a> and add it to your AI tool's
			context so it understands the full Cloudflare API surface when writing integration
			code.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2 id="documentation-mcp-server">Documentation MCP Server</h2>
	<p>
		Cloudflare runs a catalog of managed remote MCP Servers which you can
		connect to using OAuth on clients like
		<a href="https://modelcontextprotocol.io/quickstart/user">Claude</a>,
		<a href="https://docs.windsurf.com/windsurf/cascade/mcp">Windsurf</a>,
		the Cloudflare
		<a href="https://playground.ai.cloudflare.com/">AI Playground</a>, or any
		<a
			href="https://github.com/cloudflare/agents/tree/main/packages/agents/src/mcp"
			>SDK that supports MCP</a
		>.
	</p>
	<p>
		The <a
			href="https://github.com/cloudflare/mcp-server-cloudflare/tree/main/apps/docs-vectorize"
			>Documentation MCP Server</a
		> gives your AI assistant direct access to up-to-date Cloudflare documentation.
	</p>

	<h3>Install</h3>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>Cursor:</strong>
			<a
				href="https://cursor.com/en-US/install-mcp?name=cloudflare&config=eyJjb21tYW5kIjoibnB4IG1jcC1yZW1vdGUgaHR0cHM6Ly9kb2NzLm1jcC5jbG91ZGZsYXJlLmNvbS9zc2UifQ%3D%3D"
				>Direct install link</a
			>
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>VSCode:</strong>
			<a
				href="vscode:mcp/install?%7B%22name%22%3A%22cloudflare%22%2C%22url%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fdocs.mcp.cloudflare.com%2Fmcp%22%7D"
				>Direct install link</a
			>
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Manual configuration:</strong> Add the following to your MCP config:
		</li>
	</ul>
	<Code
		code={`{
  "mcpServers": {
    "cloudflare": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["mcp-remote", "https://docs.mcp.cloudflare.com/mcp"]
    }
  }
}`}
		lang="json"
	/>
	<p>
		For other MCP servers offered by Cloudflare, refer to
		<a href="/agents/model-context-protocol/mcp-servers-for-cloudflare/"
			>Cloudflare's MCP servers</a
		>.
	</p>

	<h2 id="skills">Skills</h2>
	<p>
		Cloudflare documentation supports
		<a href="https://agentskills.io/home">agent skills.</a> Agent skills are structured,
		task-specific guidance that AI tools can consume. Skills are defined in the
		<a href="https://github.com/cloudflare/skills">Cloudflare Skills repository</a>.
	</p>
	<p>To install them:</p>
	<Code code="npx skills add https://developers.cloudflare.com" lang="sh" />

	<h2 id="per-page-markdown">Per-page Markdown</h2>
	<p>
		Every documentation page is available as a lightweight Markdown page using one
		of the following methods. Both return the same output, powered by
		<a href="/fundamentals/reference/markdown-for-agents/">Markdown for Agents</a
		>.
	</p>

	<h3>Append <code>/index.md</code> to the URL</h3>
	<p>
		Add <code>/index.md</code> to the end of any page URL to get the Markdown version.
		For example:
	</p>
	<Code code="https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/get-started/index.md" lang="txt" />

	<h3>
		Send an <code>Accept: text/markdown</code> header
	</h3>
	<p>
		Request any page with the <code>Accept: text/markdown</code> header. Cloudflare's
		network converts the HTML to Markdown on the fly.
	</p>
	<Code
		code={`curl "https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/get-started/" \\
  --header "Accept: text/markdown"`}
		lang="sh"
	/>
	<p>
		The response includes an <code>x-markdown-tokens</code> header with the estimated
		token count, useful for context window planning. For more details, refer to
		<a href="/fundamentals/reference/markdown-for-agents/">Markdown for Agents</a
		>.
	</p>

	<h2 id="site-wide-endpoints">Site-wide endpoints</h2>
	<p>
		These endpoints follow the
		<a href="https://llmstxt.org/">llms.txt standard</a> and provide documentation
		content in Markdown format.
	</p>
	<table>
		<thead>
			<tr>
				<th>Endpoint</th>
				<th>Description</th>
			</tr>
		</thead>
		<tbody>
			<tr>
				<td><a href="/llms.txt"><code>/llms.txt</code></a></td>
				<td
					>Page index grouped by product category, with links to each product's
					own <code>llms.txt</code></td
				>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td><a href="/llms-full.txt"><code>/llms-full.txt</code></a></td>
				<td
					>Full content of all documentation pages in a single file, intended
					for offline indexing, bulk vectorization, or large-context models</td
				>
			</tr>
		</tbody>
	</table>

	<h2 id="per-product-endpoints">Per-product endpoints</h2>
	<p>
		Each product has its own scoped <code>llms.txt</code> and
		<code>llms-full.txt</code>. Use these for more targeted access when you only
		need documentation for a specific product.
	</p>
	<table>
		<thead>
			<tr>
				<th>Endpoint</th>
				<th>Description</th>
			</tr>
		</thead>
		<tbody>
			<tr>
				<td
					><a href="/workers/llms.txt"><code>/workers/llms.txt</code></a></td
				>
				<td>Page index for Workers documentation</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td
					><a href="/workers/llms-full.txt"
						><code>/workers/llms-full.txt</code></a
					></td
				>
				<td>Full content of all Workers documentation pages</td>
			</tr>
		</tbody>
	</table>
	<p>
		Replace <code>/workers/</code> with any product path. For the full list of available
		products, refer to <a href="/llms.txt"><code>/llms.txt</code></a>.
	</p>

	<h2 id="openapi-specification">OpenAPI specification</h2>
	<p>
		The full Cloudflare API OpenAPI specification is available for use with AI
		coding tools, API clients, or code generators.
	</p>
	<table>
		<thead>
			<tr>
				<th>Endpoint</th>
				<th>Description</th>
			</tr>
		</thead>
		<tbody>
			<tr>
				<td
					><a href="/openapi.json"><code>/openapi.json</code></a></td
				>
				<td>Full Cloudflare API OpenAPI specification (JSON)</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td
					><a href="/.well-known/api-catalog"
						><code>/.well-known/api-catalog</code></a
					></td
				>
				<td>RFC 9727 API catalog with links to the spec and documentation</td>
			</tr>
		</tbody>
	</table>
	<p>
		For the full API reference, refer to the
		<a href="/api/">Cloudflare API documentation</a>.
	</p>

	<h2 id="agents-md">AGENTS.md</h2>
	<p>
		The <code>cloudflare-docs</code> repository includes an
		<a
			href="https://github.com/cloudflare/cloudflare-docs/blob/production/AGENTS.md"
			>AGENTS.md</a
		> file that helps AI coding agents understand the structure, tooling, and conventions
		of the repository so they can make correct, buildable changes when contributing
		to documentation.
	</p>
	<p>
		AGENTS.md is a simple, open format for guiding coding agents. Refer to the
		<a href="https://agents.md/">AGENTS.md</a> website for more information.
	</p>
</StarlightPage>
